  "preamble": "Loanword adaptation of the voiced postalveolar fricative [ʒ] as the voiced alveolo-palatal fricative [ʑ]. Japanese has no postalveolar sibilants; French and English /ʒ/ is borrowed as the kana ジ/ジュ/ジャ, whose consonant is the palatalized allophone of /z/, realized [ʑ] between vowels (and [dʑ] after a pause or moraic nasal).",
